- four_sum_count([1], [1], [1], [1])
- four_sum_count([1, -1], [1, -1], [1, -1], [1, -1])
- four_sum_count([0, 0], [0, 0], [0, 0], [0, 0])
- four_sum_count([i - 10 for i in range(20)], [i - 10 for i in range(20)], [5 - i for i in range(20)], [i % 7 for i in range(20)])
fail[2]: One way: 0 + 0 + 0 + 0.
fail[3]: 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 isn't 0.
fail[4]: Two 1s and two -1s: there are 6 ways to choose which two lists give the 1s.
fail[5]: All 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 16 ways add up to 0.
fail[6]: These four lists of 20 numbers have 5790 ways.
